              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_table_3.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\">Object Hard/Soft</td><td>Material(s)</td></tr><tr><td>Brick</td><td>Hard</td><td>Baked clay</td></tr><tr><td>Water bottle</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Pillow</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Tumbler</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Table</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Sweater</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Any other</td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.435,
            0.883,
            0.478
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Compare your observations with the observations of your friends and discuss."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.481,
            0.885,
            0.566
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You have learnt that materials can have different properties, like lustre, hardness, softness and colour. Can you think of any other properties that are shown by materials? Let us explore it further."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.581,
            0.803,
            0.627
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6.3.3 Explore materials through which one can see or cannot see"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.637,
            0.884,
            0.762
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ghulan, Sheeta and Sara are playing hide and seek with their friends. Ghulan hides behind a wall, Sheeta hides behind a big tree in the garden while Sara hides behind the frosted glass door (which has a hazy surface). Sheeta’s younger brother can see all of this happening through a glass window of his house."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.761,
            0.883,
            0.822
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The materials, through which things can be seen clearly, are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "transparent",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Glass, water, air, cellophane paper, etc., are some examples of transparent materials."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.822,
            0.883,
            0.842
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Why did Ghulan, Sheeta and Sara choose these places to hide?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.842,
            0.885,
            0.905
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you think it would be possible for Sheeta’s brother to see her and her friends through a closed wooden window of the house?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
